charge\nStatement\nUCC\nRoad & Bridge\nSheriff\nTreasurer\nCommunity\nEducation\nElections & Voter Information\nHistory\nWaste Management\nBoards and Commissions\nHow Do I\nEmployment\nFull-Time Road Worker\nCommissioned Jailer/Non-Commissioned Jailer\nOpen Records Request\nContact Us\nslide 1 of 1\nContact Us\nJaimie Umhoefer\nInterim Lafayette County Auditor\nPh: (660) 259-6168\nSub Menu\nRelated Pages\nAssessor\nAuditor\nCommunity Services\nCourt\nCircuit Clerk\nAnnouncements\nChild Support\nExecution & Garnishment\nGeneral Court Information\nFAQs\nFiling Fees\nForms\nJury Duty\nLandlord Complaint Action\nMissouri Municipal Divisions\nParenting Program\nProbate Court\nRepresenting Yourself\nCounty Collector\nCounty Coroner\nCounty Clerk\nElections & Voter Information\nElection Results Archive\nFinancial Statement Publication\n8/4/26 Primary Election Results\nGIS Site\nNoxious Weed Board\nPlanning & Economic Development\nAgendas & Public Notices\nApplications, Permits & Fees\nCode Enforcement\nCommon Questions\nComprehensive Plan Maps\nEconomic Development\nFloodplain Management\nPlanning Commission & Board of Zoning Appeals\nPlanning for Lafayette County's Future\nProsecuting Attorney\nBad Checks\nChild Support Enforcement\nHistory\nVictim Services\nPublic Administrator\nPurchasing Department\nBid Opportunities\nRecorder Of Deeds\nDocument Standards\nFAQs\nFee Schedule\nMarriage License\nMilitary Discharge\nStatement\nUCC\nRoad & Bridge\nSheriff\nTreasurer\nHome\nServices\nAuditor\nCounty Auditor\nJaimie Umhoefer, Interim County Auditor\n1001 Main Street\nLexington, MO 64067\n(660) 259-6168\nEmail the Auditor's Office\nAbout the Auditor's Office\nThe Lafayette County Auditor serves as an independent financial officer responsible for promoting accountability, accuracy, and transparency in the County's financial operations.\nThe Auditor's Office works with the County Commission, elected officials, and county departments to help ensure that public funds are properly received, accounted for, and disbursed in accordance with Missouri law and generally accepted accounting practices.\nThe Auditor also serves as a financial advisor to the County Commission and coordinates preparation of the County's annual budget for review and final approval by the Commission.\nResponsibilities\nThe Auditor's Office is responsible for a variety of financial and administrative functions, including:\nReviewing claims and expenditures of county funds\nMonitoring county revenues and expenditures\nMaintaining financial and accounting records\nAssisting with preparation and administration of the annual county budget\nProviding financial information to the County Commission and county offices\nSupporting compliance with applicable Missouri statutes and accounting requirements\nCoordinating with independent auditors during the County's annual financial audit\nCounty Audit Reports\nLafayette County's annual audit reports are available below:\n2019 Audit\n2020 Audit\n2021 Audit\n2022 Audit\n2023 Audit\n2024 Audit\n×\nNo-Excuse Absentee Voting\nNo-Excuse \"Early\" Absentee Voting for the November 3rd, 2026 General Election begins on Tuesday, October 20th, 2026. The County Clerk's Office is located at 1001 Main St. Lexington, MO in the Historic Courthouse and is open M-F 8:30-4:30 with a one-hour lunch closure from Noon-1pm.\nthis page\nShare this page\n×\nCopy and paste this code into your website.\n<a href=\"http://www.lafayettecountymo.gov/services/auditor.php\">Your Link Name</a>\nShare this page on your favorite Social network\nFacebook\nTwitter\nReddit\nClose\nLafayette County Courthouse\n1001 Main St. Lexington, MO 64067\nPhone: (660) 259-4315\nRESOURCES\nCounty Commission\nAssessor\nGis\nEmployment\nContact Us\n© 2026 Lafayette County, MO\nPowered by revize. , The Government Website Experts | Login\nClose\nRead More\nOriginal text\nRate this translation\nYour feedback will be used to help improve Google Translate",
